{"level":"debug","module":"llm","time":1749861165844,"caller":"/Users/amakura/source/repos/aiup-go-gen/internal/llm/open_ai_client.go:101","message":"OpenAI response: Here’s a wireframe for the Main User Login Page of an Angular web app, expressed using a clear, text-based layout:\n\n──────────────────────────────────────────\n|             [TOP NAV BAR]              |\n|  [Logo]      App Name                  |\n|                                        |\n|  (No links on Login page to avoid      |\n|   navigation until user signs in)      |\n──────────────────────────────────────────\n\n|                                        |\n|           [MAIN CONTENT AREA]          |\n|                                        |\n|          ┌──────────────────────┐      |\n|          |      Login           |      | \n|          ├──────────────────────┤      |\n|          | Email: [__________]  |      |\n|          | Password: [______ ]  |      |\n|          |                      |      |\n|          | [Login Button]       |      |\n|          |                      |      |\n|          |  [Forgot password?]  |      |\n|          |                      |      |\n|          |----------------------|      |\n|          | [Sign Up Link]       |      |\n|          └──────────────────────┘      |\n|                                        |\n|  [Optional: Show error/success messages]|\n──────────────────────────────────────────\n\n|            [FIXED FOOTER]              |\n|    © 2024 App Name. All rights reserved.|\n|       [Privacy Policy]  [Contact]       |\n──────────────────────────────────────────\n\nSection Explanations:\n\n1. Top Nav Bar:\n   - Shows app branding/logo only, keeping navigation minimal since navigation is rarely permitted before authentication.\n   - Reinforces brand presence.\n\n2. Main Content Area:\n   - Focuses user attention on the login task.\n   - Includes labeled fields (“Email,” “Password”) with clear input boxes.\n   - Distinct, full-width “Login” button for the primary action.\n   - Secondary options for password reset (“Forgot password?” as a clickable link) and registration (“Sign Up” link).\n   - Space for concise error or confirmation messages (e.g., “Invalid password”).\n\n3. Fixed Footer:\n   - Remains at the bottom.\n   - Lightweight legal info and quick access to support/policy links.\n\nInteraction Flow:\n- User enters their credentials, clicks “Login.”\n- Errors are immediately displayed (e.g., wrong password), supporting visibility of system status.\n- Tertiary navigation (Forgot password, Sign Up) is immediately recognizable and clearly separated from the primary action.\n\nThis layout ensures a minimal, focused, and familiar login experience with strong affordances for all actions. \n\nReady for handoff to coding!"}
