{"level":"debug","module":"llm","time":1749941978244,"caller":"/Users/amakura/source/repos/aiup-go-gen/internal/llm/open_ai_client.go:72","message":"Generating response with OpenAI model for prompt: \nYou are an orchestration agent for an AI multi-agent system.\nYour job is to read the user's request and decide **which agent** should handle it next.\n\nGuidelines:\n- If the request involves UI or wireframes, FIRST send it to the \"UX Assistant\" for wireframe generation.\n- Once wireframes are complete, IMMEDIATELY hand off the next step to the \"Assistant\" agent to generate code. Do NOT assign the same subtask to the same agent repeatedly.\n- If code needs to be executed or validated, send it to the ToolRunnerAgent.\n- If the code fails verification, send the error and original request back to the \"Assistant\" agent for correction and retry.\n- When an agent's reply contains a clear handoff phrase such as \"Requesting Assistant agent to code this UI in Angular\", ALWAYS assign the next subtask to the agent mentioned in the handoff (e.g., \"Assistant\"). Never assign the same subtask to the same agent more than once unless it is a new, different subtask.\n- Repeat until the task is completed or the user explicitly stops the process.\n\nYou MUST reply ONLY with a JSON object in one of the following formats:\n- To assign: {\"agent\": \"<agent_name>\", \"subtask\": \"<task or code to perform>\"}\n- To verify code: {\"tool\": \"docker_exec\", \"args\": { \"language\": \"...\", \"code\": \"...\", ... }}\n\nAgents available:\n- Assistant \t UI Coding assistant \n- ToolRunner \t  \n- UX Assistant \t UX wireframe assistant \n\n\nUser's request:\n\"Here is a UX wireframe and explanation for the Angular login page, adhering to your specs and best practices:\n\n—————————————————————————————————————————————————————\nTOP NAVIGATION BAR\n┌───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│   [Logo/Brand]   |   Login   |   Sign Up   |   Help           │\n└───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n\nMAIN CONTENT (CENTERED LOGIN PANEL)\n┌─────────────────────────────────────┐\n│                                     │\n│        LOGIN TO YOUR ACCOUNT        │\n│ ────────────────────────────────── │\n│ [Email Address   ____________]      │\n│ [Password        ____________]      │\n│ [ ] Remember me                     │\n│                                     │\n│ [Login] [Sign in with Google]       │\n│ [Sign in with GitHub]               │\n│                                     │\n│ Forgot Password?   |   Sign Up      │\n│                                     │\n└─────────────────────────────────────┘\n\nFOOTER (FIXED)\n┌───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│  © 2024 Your Company.  Privacy Policy  |  Terms of Service   │\n└───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n\n—————————————————————————————————————————————————————\nSection Explanations:\n\n1. Top Navigation Bar:\n   - Contains a brand logo or text.\n   - Navigation links: \"Login\" (highlighted as current), \"Sign Up,\" \"Help.\"\n   - Clear, consistent placement for navigation; always visible.\n   - All links are Angular routerLinks.\n\n2. Main Content (Login Panel):\n   - Central panel for focus and accessibility.\n   - Email and Password form fields, using Angular Material components for accessible, validated input.\n   - \"Remember me\" checkbox for convenience.\n   - Primary action: [Login] button (distinguishable, disables if form invalid).\n   - Third-party login options: [Sign in with Google], [Sign in with GitHub] (elevated or outlined style for distinction; actual auth not required, just button stubs).\n   - Quick-access text links: \"Forgot Password?\" and \"Sign Up\".\n   - All elements use accessible labels and ARIA practices.\n\n3. Footer (Fixed):\n   - Stays visible at bottom of viewport.\n   - Contains copyright, privacy, and legal links.\n   - Ensures users can always find legal/info links.\n \nUser Flow:\n- User lands on login page by default.\n- Can enter credentials or pick a social login provider.\n- Can navigate to \"Sign Up\" or \"Forgot Password?\" easily.\n- Top and footer navigation always available.\n\nThis structure is designed for discoverability, clarity, and minimal distraction. The main action (login) is visually prioritized.\n\nLet me know if you want specific color palette/themes before coding. If no changes, confirm and I'll delegate to the Assistant agent to generate the full Angular code scaffold.\"\n"}
