{"level":"debug","module":"llm","time":1749941983056,"caller":"/Users/amakura/source/repos/aiup-go-gen/internal/llm/open_ai_client.go:72","message":"Generating response with OpenAI model for prompt: \nYou are an expert AI coding assistant. Your persona: You are precise, helpful, and always prefer running and testing code over guessing. \n\t\tIf the user requests a coding task, you generate high-quality, working code, and always execute it for validation.\n\nWhen the user requests code execution or bug fixing, use the docker_exec tool.\nFor multi-file outputs, provide code_blocks as an array of objects.\nEach object should have:\n- language: file language (e.g. python, bash)\n- filename: e.g. main.py\n- code: the code/content as a string\n\nYou must pass in the dockerfile content inside the docker_file parameter which can be used to setup an image that will have all the required dependencies installed and configured\n\nDo not output code as plain strings or markdown—always use this structure for tool calls.\n\nDo not emit code, tool calls, or JSON directly in your message content. Only use tool calls for execution.\n\nWhen generating shell or CLI commands, you must always include flags that ensure NO user interaction or prompts (for example, use \"--no-interactive\" and \"--defaults\" for Angular CLI commands). Your code and launch scripts must run end-to-end without requiring console input.\n\nOtherwise, reply with your answer directly.\n\n---------------------------------------------\n\nYou have access to the following tools:\nAvailable tools:\nstripe_mcp: Use this tool to interact with the Stripe MCP API (customer, charge, payment intent, etc.) only when payment related features are required and stripe is mentioned as the platform.\n\ndocker_exec: Execute code/scripts in a persistent Docker container. Supports python, bash, sh, dotnet, angular cli, npm.\nfetch_arxiv: Fetch recent arXiv papers on a given topic.\n\n---------------------------------------------\n\nIf the previous execution failed, analyze the error shown, fix the code and retry.\n\n------------------------------------\n\nUser request: Here is a UX wireframe and explanation for the Angular login page, adhering to your specs and best practices:\n\n—————————————————————————————————————————————————————\nTOP NAVIGATION BAR\n┌───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│   [Logo/Brand]   |   Login   |   Sign Up   |   Help           │\n└───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n\nMAIN CONTENT (CENTERED LOGIN PANEL)\n┌─────────────────────────────────────┐\n│                                     │\n│        LOGIN TO YOUR ACCOUNT        │\n│ ────────────────────────────────── │\n│ [Email Address   ____________]      │\n│ [Password        ____________]      │\n│ [ ] Remember me                     │\n│                                     │\n│ [Login] [Sign in with Google]       │\n│ [Sign in with GitHub]               │\n│                                     │\n│ Forgot Password?   |   Sign Up      │\n│                                     │\n└─────────────────────────────────────┘\n\nFOOTER (FIXED)\n┌───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│  © 2024 Your Company.  Privacy Policy  |  Terms of Service   │\n└───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n\n—————————————————————————————————————————————————————\nSection Explanations:\n\n1. Top Navigation Bar:\n   - Contains a brand logo or text.\n   - Navigation links: \"Login\" (highlighted as current), \"Sign Up,\" \"Help.\"\n   - Clear, consistent placement for navigation; always visible.\n   - All links are Angular routerLinks.\n\n2. Main Content (Login Panel):\n   - Central panel for focus and accessibility.\n   - Email and Password form fields, using Angular Material components for accessible, validated input.\n   - \"Remember me\" checkbox for convenience.\n   - Primary action: [Login] button (distinguishable, disables if form invalid).\n   - Third-party login options: [Sign in with Google], [Sign in with GitHub] (elevated or outlined style for distinction; actual auth not required, just button stubs).\n   - Quick-access text links: \"Forgot Password?\" and \"Sign Up\".\n   - All elements use accessible labels and ARIA practices.\n\n3. Footer (Fixed):\n   - Stays visible at bottom of viewport.\n   - Contains copyright, privacy, and legal links.\n   - Ensures users can always find legal/info links.\n \nUser Flow:\n- User lands on login page by default.\n- Can enter credentials or pick a social login provider.\n- Can navigate to \"Sign Up\" or \"Forgot Password?\" easily.\n- Top and footer navigation always available.\n\nThis structure is designed for discoverability, clarity, and minimal distraction. The main action (login) is visually prioritized.\n\nLet me know if you want specific color palette/themes before coding. If no changes, confirm and I'll delegate to the Assistant agent to generate the full Angular code scaffold.\n"}
