ch file in its own fenced code block.\n- Do not mix multiple files into one code block.\n- Generate a launch.sh bash script to launch the angular application.\n- *Always output the launch.sh script file following any changes to the codebase to ensure executor runs successful test of full API.*\n\n## Additonal text in output\n- When including any extra comments or chain of thought reasoning whilst resolving issues, this must only be included in the following format:\n\n    ###BEGIN_LLM_COMMENTS\n    Your comments or notes here, in plain text.\n    ###END_LLM_COMMENTS\n\n- Do not include these boundary markers in any other context. Do not reveal hidden chain-of-thought outside these markers.\n\n## Environment Variables\nUse the following environment variables where needed:\n    AZURE_CLIENTID\n    AZURE_APIID\n    AZURE_AUTHORITY\n    AZURE_TENANT\n    AZURE_POLICY\n    AZURE_SCOPE\n    API_BASE_URL\n\n## Error Flow\n- If the docker executor indicates an error (non-zero exit code), revise the entire code\n\nFor all code execution or bug fixing, use the docker_exec tool.\nFor multi-file outputs, provide code_blocks as an array of objects.\nEach object should have:\n- language: file language (e.g. python, bash, typescript)\n- filename: e.g. service.ts\n- code: the code/content as a string\n\nYou must pass in the dockerfile content inside the docker_file parameter which can be used to setup an image that will have all the required dependencies installed and configured\n\nDo not output code as plain strings or markdown—always use this structure for tool calls.\n\nDo not emit code, tool calls, or JSON directly in your message content. Only use tool calls for execution.\n\nWhen generating shell or CLI commands, you must always include flags that ensure NO user interaction or prompts (for example, use \"--no-interactive\" and \"--defaults\" for Angular CLI commands). Your code and launch scripts must run end-to-end without requiring console input.\n\nOtherwise, reply with your answer directly.\n\n---------------------------------------------\n\nYou have access to the following tools:\n%s\n\n---------------------------------------------\n\nIf the previous execution failed, analyze the error shown, fix the code and retry.\n\n------------------------------------\n\nUser request: %s\n\n \n\n Below is a recommended wireframe for the \"User Login Page\" of your Angular web app, following UX best practices and your stated requirements.\n\n─────────────────────────────────────────────\n[TOP NAVIGATION BAR]  \n[   App Logo   ]               [ Help | Contact | Settings ]  \n\n─────────────────────────────────────────────\n[ MAIN CONTENT AREA — Centered Login Panel ]  \n\n   +--------------------------------------+\n   |          User Login                  |\n   +--------------------------------------+\n   |                                      |\n   |  [ Email Address      ]  (input)      |\n   |  [ Password           ]  (input)      |\n   |                                      |\n   |  [  Log In  ]  (primary button)      |\n   |                                      |\n   |  [ Forgot Password? ] (link)          |\n   |                                      |\n   |  —————————  or  ————————              |\n   |                                      |\n   |  [ Log In with Google ] (button)      |\n   |  [ Log In with SSO    ] (button)      |\n   |                                      |\n   |  [ Don't have an account? ]           |\n   |  [ Sign up ] (link)                   |\n   +--------------------------------------+\n\n─────────────────────────────────────────────\n[ FIXED FOOTER ]  \n[ Terms | Privacy | © 2024 YourApp ]        \n\n\nSection explanations and user interactions:\n\n1. **Top Navigation Bar**  \n   - Includes the application logo/brand name (left) and minimal utility links (Help, Contact, Settings) right-aligned.  \n   - Since this is a login page, navigation is intentionally minimal to avoid distractions.\n\n2. **Main Content Area**  \n   - Centered \"User Login\" panel, keeping primary focus for quick form completion.  \n   - Includes labeled input fields for \"Email Address\" and \"Password.\"\n   - Clear, prominent \"Log In\" button (primary CTA).\n   - A secondary link for password recovery (\"Forgot Password?\").\n   - Optional alternative login methods below a visual separator (e.g., Google, SSO, etc.), to accommodate multiple authentication strategies.\n   - A prompt and link for a new user to create an account (\"Sign up\").\n   - Inputs are properly labeled for accessibility and clarity.\n   - Extra buttons (Google/SSO) can be omitted or disabled if not needed initially.\n\n3. **Fixed Footer**  \n   - Persistent at the bottom for legal or informational links (Terms, Privacy, copyright).\n   - Only essential details to avoid clutter.\n\n**Navigation and Flow:**  \n- Users land on the login screen, fill email/password, and hit \"Log In.\"  \n- If login fails, an inline error message appears under the fields.\n- Forgotten passwords or new users are guided with brief, scannable links.\n- Alternative login methods are easy to spot below the main form.\n- Minimal distractions keep user focused on login.\n\nThis layout provides a clean, professional first impression, clear flows for returning or new users, and accommodates expansion for additional auth providers. \n\nDo you want to proceed with an Angular code implementation for this login page?"}
