ort                                 |\n────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n---\n\nSection Explanations:\n\n1. Top Navigation Bar:\n   - Placed at the very top and contains the application logo on the left.\n   - The right side features the current page (\"Login\"), visually indicating to the user where they are.\n   - Designed for consistency so future links (e.g., \"Dashboard\") can be easily added.\n\n2. Main Content:\n   - Centralized login form, visually prioritized.\n   - Prominent heading (\"Welcome Back!\") introduces the purpose of this page.\n   - Fields for email and password, each in its own input box.\n   - A clear \"Login\" button is displayed prominently.\n   - \"Forgot Password?\" link below or beside the password field for account recovery.\n   - Under the form, a minimal prompt and button to \"Sign Up\" if the user has no account.\n   - All interactive elements are clearly labeled, with noticeable affordances (i.e., buttons and links distinguished from static text).\n\n3. Fixed Footer:\n   - Stays at the bottom of the screen.\n   - Contains secondary navigation: copyright, privacy policy, and support.\n   - Provides users with access to help or legal at any time.\n\nNavigation & Usability:\n- Clear navigation path: no distractions; the only main action is logging in or signing up.\n- Buttons and links are visually prominent for easy discoverability.\n- Consistent structure for brand and navigation, even on a single-function page like login.\n\nThis wireframe is now ready to move to the UI coding phase."}
