{"level":"debug","module":"llm","time":1750291680366,"caller":"/Users/amakura/source/repos/aiup-go-gen/internal/llm/open_ai_client.go:156","message":"OpenAI response: Certainly! Let's begin with creating a wireframe for the web application's landing page, which will serve as a \"Dashboard.\" The objective is to provide a foundational design that includes navigation, key sections, and user interaction points for a platform where users can view system status, manage entities, and navigate effectively. \n\nHere's a sample text-based wireframe outlining the dashboard layout:\n\n```\n-----------------------------------------------\n| Top Navigation Bar                          |\n|---------------------------------------------|\n| Home / Dashboard | Appointments | Search   |\n| Settings                                  |\n-----------------------------------------------\n|                                             |\n| Sidebar Navigation (optional)               |\n|---------------------------------------------|\n| - Overview                                  |\n| - History                                   |\n|                                             |\n-----------------------------------------------\n|                                             |\n| Main Content Area                           |\n|---------------------------------------------|\n| Status Overview                             |\n| - Total Entities: [Number]                  |\n| - Upcoming: [Next Appointment Date/Time]    |\n|---------------------------------------------|\n| + New Appointment                     |>    |\n|                                             |\n| Entity List or Grid                         |\n|---------------------------------------------|\n| [Entity 1] Edit | Delete                    |\n| [Entity 2] Edit | Delete                    |\n| [Entity 3] Edit | Delete                    |\n| ...                                         |\n|---------------------------------------------|\n| Page Navigation: < Previous | Next >        |\n-----------------------------------------------\n|                                             |\n| Fixed Footer (quick links/disclaimers)      |\n|---------------------------------------------|\n| © Year SiteName - Privacy | Terms           |\n-----------------------------------------------\n```\n\n**Explanation:**\n\n1. **Top Navigation Bar**: This horizontal bar serves as the primary means for navigating different sections of the application, such as \"Home/Dashboard,\" \"Appointments,\" \"Search,\" and \"Settings.\"\n\n2. **Sidebar Navigation (Optional)**: This may contain more granular navigation options related to sections within the dashboard, like \"Overview\" and \"History.\"\n\n3. **Main Content Area**: \n   - **Status Overview**: Provides a quick glance at essential metrics like total entities and upcoming events.\n   - **+ New Appointment**: A prominent call-to-action button to add new entities or appointments.\n   - **Entity List or Grid**: Displays the current entities with options to \"Edit\" or \"Delete\" each entry. \n   - **Page Navigation**: Allows users to navigate between pages of entities.\n\n4. **Fixed Footer**: Contains quick links or necessary disclaimers and remains consistent at the bottom of the page.\n\nThis wireframe will be the base for the UI and interactions, ensuring user-friendly navigation and management of entities within the web application. Now, I'll delegate this to the Assistant agent for coding up."}
