you must always include flags that ensure NO user interaction or prompts (for example, use \"--no-interactive\" and \"--defaults\" for Angular CLI commands). Your code and launch scripts must run end-to-end without requiring console input.\n\nOtherwise, reply with your answer directly.\n\n---------------------------------------------\n\nYou have access to the following tools:\n%s\n\n---------------------------------------------\n\nIf the previous execution failed, analyze the error shown, fix the code and retry.\n\n------------------------------------\n\nUser request: %s\n\n\n\nYou have access to the following tools:\nAvailable tools:\nstripe_mcp: Use this tool to interact with the Stripe MCP API (customer, charge, payment intent, etc.) only when payment related features are required and stripe is mentioned as the platform.\n\ndocker_exec: Execute code/scripts in a persistent Docker container. Supports python, bash, sh, dotnet, angular cli, npm.\n\nUser request: \n    [ERROR: Docker Exec - LAUNCH phase]\n    Command:\n    bash create_app.sh\n\n    Output/Error:\n    chmod: cannot access 'launch.sh': No such file or directory\n\n\n    Internal error: exit status 1\n    \n\n---------------------------\n\n\n\n* IMPORTANT: If you produce a reply, you MUST reply only in strict JSON. Output nothing else, nor do not include any leading text or comments. Just return valid JSON objects:\nN.B Do not use any backticks or ``` as this will be marshalled as a string in the JSON using 'Go', so string content must be compatible.\n\nFormat your output like this json object:\n{\n\t\"role\": \"ux\",\n\t\"type\": \"wireframe\",\n\t\"content\": \"ASCII wireframe and explanation here, without any ```\", \n\t\"route_target\": \"assistant\"\n}\n\t\nEnsure this output is valid JSON:\n- You must escape all newlines embedded in the content as \\n \n- Replace or encode any strange characters such as backticks, so that it can be easily parsed in Go.\n- Do not use any other format or free text, only valid JSON objects.\n\n\n*\tUse type: \"tool_call\" and set \"route_target\": \"toolrunner\" when code execution is needed.\n*\tOnly return with no route_target if the process is fully done.\n\n\n\nPREVIOUS TOOL ERROR:\n\n    [ERROR: Docker Exec - LAUNCH phase]\n    Command:\n    bash create_app.sh\n\n    Output/Error:\n    chmod: cannot access 'launch.sh': No such file or directory\n\n\n    Internal error: exit status 1\n    \n\nError Phase: tool_call\nTool Name: docker_exec\nError Detail: init failed: exit status 1\n\n\n# Previous request context:\nLogin Page Wireframe:\n\n---------------------------------------------\n|                                             |\n|                Company Logo                 |\n|                                             |\n---------------------------------------------\n|                                             |\n|             [ Username:         ]            |\n|             [ Password:          ]           |\n|                                             |\n|    [ Remember Me ]                         |\n|                                             |\n|    [ Login Button ]                        |\n|                                             |\n|             [ Forgot Password? ]             |\n|                                             |\n|                                             |\n---------------------------------------------\n|                                             |\n|  Don't have an account? [ Sign Up Here ]    |\n|                                             |\n---------------------------------------------\n\nExplanation:\n- **Company Logo:** This shall be a placeholder for the company logo, providing branding and familiarity to the user.\n- **Username & Password Fields:** Input fields for the user to enter their login credentials.\n- **Remember Me Checkbox:** Option for users to save login information for future convenience.\n- **Login Button:** Primary call-to-action for users to submit their credentials and access their account.\n- **Forgot Password Link:** Allows users to reset their password if they cannot remember it.\n- **Sign Up Link:** For users who do not have an account, this link directs them to account creation.\n\nNavigation and interaction are kept minimal since the login page's purpose is simply authentication. Clear calls-to-action are present for users to log in, recover credentials, or register for a new account if needed.\n"}
